# Laundry Services Website

## Project Overview

This project is a responsive **Laundry Services Website** developed using **HTML5 and CSS3**. The website provides a clean and simple user interface for a laundry service. It contains a navigation bar, laundry service information, booking button, responsive layout, and laundry-related image.

The website is designed to work on desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes using CSS media queries.

## Technologies Used

* HTML5
* CSS3
* Flexbox
* CSS Media Queries
* Responsive Web Design

## Features

* Responsive navigation header
* Website logo
* Home, Services, About Us, and Contact Us links
* Username button
* Mobile hamburger menu
* Responsive hero section
* Laundry service heading
* Service description
* Book a service button
* Laundry machine image
* Mobile and tablet responsive design
* Image alternative text using `alt`

## Project Structure

```text
Laundry-Services/
│
├── index.html
├── style2.css
├── image.png
└── README.md
```

## File Description

### index.html

This file contains the main structure of the website.

It includes:

* Header
* Logo
* Navigation menu
* Username button
* Hamburger menu
* Hero section
* Laundry service content
* Booking button
* Laundry image

### style2.css

This file contains the complete styling of the webpage.

It controls:

* Layout
* Colors
* Fonts
* Navigation
* Buttons
* Hero section
* Image size and position
* Mobile menu
* Responsive design

### image.png

This image is displayed in the hero section and represents the laundry service.

## Responsive Design

The website uses CSS media queries to adjust the design according to screen size.

### Tablet / Small Screen

```css
@media (max-width: 770px) and (max-height: 1024px)
```

This changes the font sizes, spacing, image size, button size, and overall layout for smaller screens.

### Mobile Screen

```css
@media (max-width: 376px) and (max-height: 751px)
```

On smaller mobile devices:

* Navigation links are hidden.
* Hamburger menu is displayed.
* Hero section becomes vertical.
* Image size is reduced.
* Text size is adjusted.
* Booking button is resized.

## Mobile Navigation

The hamburger menu is implemented using CSS.

```css
.hamburgerMenu:focus + .mobile-nav {
    display: flex;
}
```

When the hamburger button receives focus, the mobile navigation menu becomes visible.

## Accessibility

The laundry image includes alternative text:

```html
<img class="Image" src="image.png" alt="Laundry Machine Image">
```

The `alt` attribute provides a text description of the image for users using screen readers.

## How to Run

1. Create a folder named `Laundry-Services`.
2. Add `index.html`, `style2.css`, and `image.png` to the folder.
3. Open the folder in VS Code.
4. Make sure the CSS and image file paths are correct.
5. Open `index.html` in a browser.
6. You can also use VS Code Live Server to run the project.

